{
  "provider": {
    "version": 0,
    "block": {
      "attributes": {
        "api_key": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "A Headscale api key.",
          "description_kind": "plain",
          "optional": true,
          "sensitive": true
        },
        "endpoint": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Headscale endpoint to connect to. (e.g. `https://headscale.example.com`)",
          "description_kind": "markdown",
          "optional": true
        }
      },
      "description": "The Headscale provider allow you to manage various resources and retrieve data of existing resources on a Headscale instance. To utilize this provider, you must have a valid API key and a Headscale instance with a valid TLS certificate. You can generate an API key by running `headscale apikey create` on the Headscale instance.\n\nThe Headscale endpoint and API key can be specified in the provider block or by setting the `HEADSCALE_ENDPOINT` and `HEADSCALE_API_KEY` environment variables.",
      "description_kind": "markdown"
    }
  },
  "resource_schemas": {
    "headscale_api_key": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time the key was created.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "expiration": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Expiration date of the api key.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "expired": {
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "If the api key is expired.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The id of the api key.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "key": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The api key.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true,
            "sensitive": true
          },
          "prefix": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The api key's prefix.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "time_to_expire": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time until the key expires. This is a string in the format of `30m`, `3h`, `90d`, etc. Defaults to `90d`",
            "description_kind": "markdown",
            "optional": true
          }
        },
        "description": "The API key resource allows you to create an API key that can be used to interact with the Headscale API. By default keys that are created with this resource will expire in 90 days. Keys cannot be modified, so any change to the input on this resource will cause the key to be expired and a new key to be created.",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
    "headscale_device_subnet_routes": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "device_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The id of the device to get subnet routes from.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The Terraform Id of the resource.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "routes": {
            "type": [
              "list",
              "string"
            ],
            "description": "The enabled routes of the device.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          }
        },
        "description": "The device subnet routes resource allows enabling routes advertised by a device registered on the Headscale instance. Utilizing this resource will reset any previous configuration for routes advertised by the device. If a route was previously enabled but is not present in the list of routes, it will be disabled.",
        "description_kind": "plain"
      }
    },
    "headscale_device_tags": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "device_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The id of the device to set tags on.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The resolved id of the device.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "tags": {
            "type": [
              "list",
              "string"
            ],
            "description": "The tags applied to the device.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          }
        },
        "description": "The device tags resource allows setting tags on a device registered on the Headscale instance. Utilizing this resource will reset any previous configuration for tags applied to the device. If a tag was previously applied but is not present in the list of tags, it will be removed.",
        "description_kind": "plain"
      }
    },
    "headscale_policy": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The Terraform Id of the resource.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "policy": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The policy data in HuJSON format. See https://tailscale.com/kb/1337/policy-syntax.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "updated": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time when the policy was last updated.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          }
        },
        "description": "The policy resource allows definition of the ACL policy used for the tailnet. To use this resource, the Headscale instance must have the `policy.mode` setting set to `database`.\n\nTo read more about ACL policies, see the [Tailscale documentation](https://tailscale.com/kb/1018/acls).",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
    "headscale_pre_auth_key": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "acl_tags": {
            "type": [
              "set",
              "string"
            ],
            "description": "ACL tags on the pre auth key.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time the key was created.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "ephemeral": {
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "If the key is ephemeral.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "expiration": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time the pre auth key expires at.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "expired": {
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "If the key is expired.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The id of the pre auth key.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "key": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The pre auth key.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true,
            "sensitive": true
          },
          "reusable": {
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "If the key is reusable.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "time_to_expire": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time until the key expires. This is a string in the format of `30m`, `3h`, `90d`, etc. Defaults to `1h`",
            "description_kind": "markdown",
            "optional": true
          },
          "used": {
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "If the key has been used.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "user": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The ID of the user that will own the pre auth key. Omit this for tags-only keys on Headscale v0.28.0+.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          }
        },
        "description": "The pre auth key resource allows you to create a pre auth key that can be used to register a new device on the Headscale instance. By default keys that are created with this resource will be not reusable, not ephemeral, and expire in 1 hour. Keys cannot be modified, so any change to the input on this resource will cause the key to be replaced.",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
    "headscale_user": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The time the user was created.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "display_name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The display name of the user.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true
          },
          "email": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The email address of the user.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true
          },
          "force_delete": {
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "If the user should be deleted even if it has nodes attached to it. Defaults to `false`.",
            "description_kind": "markdown",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The user's id.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The name of the user.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "profile_picture_url": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The URL of the user's profile picture.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true
          }
        },
        "description": "The user resource allows you to register a user on the Headscale instance.",
        "description_kind": "plain"
      }
    }
  },
